{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בדרך לשטן", :translit "b'derekh l'satan", :gloss "on the road, as an adversary"} {:he "מכאן שכל הדרכים בחזקת סכנה", :translit "mikan shekhol ha-derakhim b'chezkat sakanah", :gloss "from here that all roads are presumed dangerous"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Halakhic inference: the word לשטן attached to בדרך teaches that travel carries a presumption of danger."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud lists travel among activities with inherent danger, placing journeys alongside other recognized hazards (Shabbat 82a). A separate discussion addresses which forms of travel require abbreviated prayer, treating roads as inherently risky (Berakhot 16a, 30a). The phrase 'as an adversary' attached to Balaam's journey demonstrates this principle from the verse itself: the road creates an opening for danger and divine opposition.", :sources ["Shabbat 82a" "Berakhot 16a" "Berakhot 30a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Halakhic inference: the word לשטן attached to בדרך teaches that travel carries a presumption of danger.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:46.329852815Z", :model "glm-5.2"}